From 898b1ad07a546829b40a4ae226e0d08c8bca2568 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joaco2382 <104966815+Joaco2382@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 11:12:17 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] fix: rest the pointer at the center when there's no mouse
 input

With --disable-mouse the input drivers report 0, 0, so scenes treated the
pointer as sitting in the bottom left corner: camera parallax shifted the
whole scene and left part of the screen empty (workshop 1982331270 showed a
grey band and the wrong part of the image). The first frame also ran before
the visible part of the scene was worked out (all UVs 0), so even with
input the parallax started from a corner and took seconds to settle, which
with a large parallaxDepth (50 in workshop 2069970082) left a band empty.

The pointer now rests at the center of what's visible when mouse input is
off, and at the center of the scene until the visible part is known.

Tests: ScenePointer (3 cases).
